issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118233","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118233","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118233.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118233.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"<!--\r\nPlease target the `master` branch. We will take care of backporting relevant fixes to older versions.\r\n\r\nBefore submitting, please read our checklist for new contributors:\r\nhttps://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/engine/introduction.html#checklist-for-new-contributors\r\n-->\r\nThe pull request is to correct the bug #118178, which raise the issue that resizeing a DrawableTexture2D would not update the texture size.\r\n\r\nI just added an _initialize(), which reinitialize the texture, when you set either width or height. Otherwise the texture remained the same size.\r\n\r\nI checked a few textures implementations and none of them implemented the size setter. \r\n \r\nI tested in the UI, and it reset the texture, but once Update is pressed, the texture has the correct behavior and size.\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"Geek-Nb-One","id":128151604,"node_id":"U_kgDOB6NwNA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128151604?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Geek-Nb-One","html_url":"https://github.com/Geek-Nb-One","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Geek-Nb-One/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Geek-Nb-One/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Geek-Nb-One/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Geek-Nb-One/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Geek-Nb-One/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Geek-Nb-One/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Geek-Nb-One/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.